libavformat: take the picture size of a video stream from its parser

FFmpeg n6.0.1 only learns the width and height of H.264 and HEVC from the
decoder. The command line tool has no decoders, so a stream copy of RTSP into
Matroska failed with "dimensions not set" (MPEG-TS does not store them). The
parsers already compute the size from the SPS: copy it into the stream
parameters when nothing else set them.

Modified by easiptv-ffmpeg on 2026-11-17, for the command line tool
(build-cli.sh) only: the audio decoder (build-decoder.sh) builds the
unmodified FFmpeg n6.0.1.

--- a/libavformat/demux.c
+++ b/libavformat/demux.c
@@ -1141,6 +1141,14 @@
                                &out_pkt->data, &out_pkt->size, data, size,
                                pkt->pts, pkt->dts, pkt->pos);
 
+        /* Without a decoder only the parser knows the picture size (H.264, HEVC);
+         * a stream copy into a muxer that stores it (Matroska) needs it. */
+        if (st->codecpar->codec_type == AVMEDIA_TYPE_VIDEO && !sti->avctx->width &&
+            sti->parser->width > 0 && sti->parser->height > 0) {
+            sti->avctx->width  = sti->parser->width;
+            sti->avctx->height = sti->parser->height;
+        }
+
         pkt->pts = pkt->dts = AV_NOPTS_VALUE;
         pkt->pos = -1;
         /* increment read pointer */
